-- title:
--   Terminal choices enumerate exactly the required suffix subsets
-- statement:
--   Let $h,J\in\mathbb N$ and let $q$ be a global output with a $2h$-element row $Q_i$ in each block $i<J$, whose local ground set has size $512h$. For $k\in\mathbb N$, let $R_k$ contain the coordinates of these rows in all blocks $i\ge k$. The terminal choice list enumerates subsets of the remaining query coordinates of the prescribed size. For any coordinate set $S$,
--
--   $$S\in\operatorname{Choices}(q,k)\iff S\subseteq R_k\ \land\ |S|=(J-k)h.$$
--
--   Subtraction is natural-number subtraction, so the statement includes $k>J$. This characterizes the completions considered by the actual terminal enumerator.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/ReportingHostTerminalChoices.lean#L42-L57

